{"id":"P01","category":"rail_code","question":"What does `head []` return in Rail?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"Per docs, head [] is defined to return 0 (runtime safety guarantee).","rail_claim":"head []","rail_claim_output":"0"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Ran it. Returns 0.","rail_claim":"head []","rail_claim_output":"0"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"Defined behavior is a wart; should be undefined.","rail_claim":"head []","rail_claim_output":"undefined"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P02","category":"rail_code","question":"Will `fold + 0 (range 1000000)` overflow the stack?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"TCO is documented; should not overflow.","rail_claim":"fold + 0 (range 1000000)","rail_claim_output":"499999500000"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Ran it. Completes in ~20ms.","rail_claim":"fold + 0 (range 1000000)","rail_claim_output":"499999500000"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"What if TCO is broken on this branch?","rail_claim":"fold + 0 (range 1000000)","rail_claim_output":"stack overflow"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P03","category":"reasoning","question":"Does `add x y = x + y` preserve referential transparency on all 64-bit integers?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"Yes, addition is total on ints.","rail_claim":"add 2 3","rail_claim_output":"5"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Tested on common inputs, always works.","rail_claim":"add 2 3","rail_claim_output":"5"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"Overflow on max_int wraps, breaks purity.","rail_claim":"add 9223372036854775807 1","rail_claim_output":"-9223372036854775808"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P04","category":"reasoning","question":"What is `1+1` in this expression language?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"Arithmetic addition: 2.","rail_claim":"1+1","rail_claim_output":"int-2"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Default reading is integer addition.","rail_claim":"1+1","rail_claim_output":"int-2"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"In a string-coercing language, could be concat.","rail_claim":"str(1)++str(1)","rail_claim_output":"str-11"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P05","category":"rail_code","question":"Is `map f []` equal to `[]`?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"Yes, by definition of map on the empty list.","rail_claim":"map (\\x -> x*2) []","rail_claim_output":"[]"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Tested. Returns [].","rail_claim":"map (\\x -> x*2) []","rail_claim_output":"[]"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"What if f has side effects? Still []?","rail_claim":"map (\\x -> error \"side\") []","rail_claim_output":"error: side"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P06","category":"reasoning","question":"Is the empty sum (sum of []) equal to 0?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"Yes, 0 is the identity element of +.","rail_claim":"fold + 0 []","rail_claim_output":"0"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Returns 0 in standard libs.","rail_claim":"fold + 0 []","rail_claim_output":"0"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"Depends on the additive monoid chosen.","rail_claim":"fold + 0 []","rail_claim_output":"depends on monoid"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P07","category":"rail_code","question":"What does `length \"abc\"` return \u2014 3 chars or 3 bytes?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"length on string returns char count.","rail_claim":"length (chars \"abc\")","rail_claim_output":"3"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Tested ASCII, returns 3.","rail_claim":"length (chars \"abc\")","rail_claim_output":"3"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"For UTF-8 with multibyte chars, char count != byte count.","rail_claim":"length (chars \"\u00e9\")","rail_claim_output":"1"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P08","category":"reasoning","question":"Is recursion equivalent to iteration?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"With TCO, tail recursion compiles to iteration. Otherwise no.","rail_claim":"church_encode_recursion_as_loop","rail_claim_output":"yes-with-tco"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Tested loop vs tail-recursive sum; same perf with TCO.","rail_claim":"benchmark_loop_vs_tail_rec","rail_claim_output":"identical-with-tco"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"Non-tail recursion uses stack; not equivalent.","rail_claim":"non_tail_recursive_fib 40","rail_claim_output":"stack-grows-linearly"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
{"id":"P09","category":"rail_code","question":"Does `x == x` always evaluate to true?","panel":[{"mode":"deductive","prose":"Reflexivity of equality.","rail_claim":"5 == 5","rail_claim_output":"true"},{"mode":"empirical","prose":"Tested ints, strings, lists. Always true.","rail_claim":"\"a\" == \"a\"","rail_claim_output":"true"},{"mode":"adversarial","prose":"NaN != NaN in IEEE 754 floats.","rail_claim":"nan == nan","rail_claim_output":"false"}],"ground_truth":"productive"}
